---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../../components/PageHero.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="Your own storefront. The same stock behind it." description="A planned Kora-powered website connected to the inventory and orders you already manage.">
<PageHero eyebrow="The Kora product plan" title="Your own storefront. The same stock behind it." lede="A planned Kora-powered website connected to the inventory and orders you already manage." />
<section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-14 prose-kora">
<h2>Set up the business once</h2>
<p>The storefront will draw products, variants and prices from your Kora catalogue. Customers can browse, choose a variant and place an order through supported checkout.</p>
<h2>Checkout checks again</h2>
<p>A product page can become stale. The backend must check availability and reserve stock again at checkout, then handle payment, hold expiry and fulfilment.</p>
<h2>A focused store before a full builder</h2>
<p>Start with a small set of useful templates, product pages, a cart and checkout. A large drag-and-drop builder, marketplace and custom integration for every platform are separate projects.</p>
<h2>For existing online stores</h2>
<p>Selected Shopify or WooCommerce connectors are on the roadmap. Each needs clear ownership of products and stock, plus recovery when updates fail. No existing-store connector is active here.</p>
<p><a href="/pilot" class="btn btn-primary">Explore the founding pilot</a></p>
</section>
</BaseLayout>
